---
description: AI FDE rules for the CGT brownfield capstone
alwaysApply: true
---
1. Treat every patient/material/batch relationship as evidence-bearing and potentially inconsistent.
2. Do not assume latest timestamp equals latest real-world event.
3. Do not collapse QC complete, QA released, product ready, and infusion ready into one status.
4. Prefer bounded autonomy: observe/correlate/recommend before consequential action.
5. Every cross-system write must consider idempotency, compensation and audit evidence.
6. Keep fixes narrow; do not clean intentional challenge data without a requirement.
7. Add or update tests and document any changed assumptions.
